		<ol id="e01597">
			<li>
				<p>To install Universal CRS, 1st row passenger seatback should be up at most upright position.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>To install R3 size CRS. 
					<ul id="e01598">
						<li>
							<p>Front Driver Seat: Seat Height should be up highest position.</p>
						</li>
						<li>
							<p>Front Passenger Seat: Seat should be moved foremost position.</p>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p>Never place a rearward facing Child Restraint System on the front passenger seat, unless the air bag is deactivated.</p>
		<p>For semi-universal or vehicle specific CRS (ISOFIX or belted CRS), please see the vehicle list provided in the manual of CRS.</p>
		<p>If the vehicle headrest prevents proper installation of a CRS, the headrest of the seating position shall be readjusted or entirely removed.</p>
		<p>When Installing Child Restraint system on 2nd row seats, move the seat to mid-position.</p>
